2. THE PROBLEM WE ARE SOLVING\par
\par
We run one Google Ads Search campaign with a daily budget of R$ 25.\par
The campaign sends traffic to a content page that answers the query the\par
user typed, and from there to our sign-up flow.\par
\par
The Google Ads interface tells us how many people CLICKED and how many\par
SIGNED UP. It cannot tell us who PAID, because payment happens days later\par
through Asaas, our Brazilian payment gateway, entirely outside Google's\par
systems.\par
\par
With a budget this small, the difference matters: a keyword that produces\par
many free sign-ups and no paying customers must be paused, and a keyword\par
that produces few sign-ups but converts them into subscriptions must be\par
funded. Today we cannot tell those two apart.\par
\par
\par
3. THE TOOL\par
\par
An internal, read-only reporting page inside our own product, available\par
only on localhost to the company owner. It is not a public feature, it is\par
not sold, and it is not accessible to our customers.\par
\par
The page already exists for Meta Ads (implemented at\par
lib/dono/meta-ads.ts) and returns HTTP 404 when the request does not come\par
from localhost, enforced in lib/dono/somente-local.ts. The Google Ads\par
section will follow the exact same pattern.\par
\par
3.1 What it displays\par
\par
  - Campaign, ad group and keyword performance:\par
    impressions, clicks, average CPC, cost, conversions\par
  - A 30-day daily cost series\par
  - Cost per sign-up and cost per paying customer, per keyword\par
\par
3.2 How the data is joined\par
\par
  Google Ads appends a click identifier (GCLID) to our landing page URL.\par
  Our application stores it on the workspace record when the account is\par
  created (database migration 0071, column workspaces.gclid), together\par
  with the UTM parameters.\par
\par
  Our own database already records whether a workspace later became a\par
  paying subscriber, through our payment gateway webhook.\par
\par
  The tool therefore joins:\par
    Google Ads API  ->  spend and clicks per keyword\par
    our database    ->  GCLID -> workspace -> paid subscription\par
\par
  and produces the only metric that decides whether the campaign\par
  continues: cost per PAYING customer, per keyword.\par
\par
\par
4. API USAGE\par
\par
4.1 Services used\par
\par
  GoogleAdsService.SearchStream, read-only.\par
  No mutate operations of any kind. We will not create, modify, pause or\par
  delete campaigns, ad groups, ads, keywords or budgets through the API.\par
  All campaign management is done by hand in the Google Ads web interface.\par
\par
4.2 Resources queried\par
\par
  customer\par
  campaign\par
  ad_group\par
  ad_group_criterion (keyword text and match type)\par
  metrics (impressions, clicks, average_cpc, cost_micros, conversions)\par
  segments.date\par
\par
4.3 Example query\par
\par
  SELECT\par
    campaign.name,\par
    ad_group.name,\par
    ad_group_criterion.keyword.text,\par
    ad_group_criterion.keyword.match_type,\par
    metrics.impressions,\par
    metrics.clicks,\par
    metrics.average_cpc,\par
    metrics.cost_micros,\par
    metrics.conversions,\par
    segments.date\par
  FROM keyword_view\par
  WHERE segments.date DURING LAST_30_DAYS\par
\par
4.4 Volume\par
\par
  One account. Approximately 2 to 10 requests per day, triggered manually\par
  when the owner opens the internal page. There is no polling loop and no\par
  scheduled job. Expected volume is far below the Basic Access limit.\par
\par
4.5 Authentication\par
\par
  OAuth 2.0 with a refresh token belonging to the account owner, stored in\par
  a local environment file that is excluded from version control. The\par
  developer token is stored the same way. Neither value is committed to\par
  our repository, shipped to the browser, or deployed to our hosting\par
  provider.\par
\par
\par
5. ACCESS AND DATA HANDLING\par
\par
  Who has access: internal only. One person, the company owner. The page\par
  is unreachable from the public internet by design.\par
\par
  What we store: aggregated performance metrics only (counts, costs,\par
  keyword text). We do not request, store or process any end-user\par
  personal data through the Google Ads API.\par
\par
  We do not use the App Conversion Tracking and Remarketing API.\par
\par
  We do not use a tool developed by a third party. The integration is\par
  written and maintained by us, in TypeScript, inside our own codebase.\par
\par
\par
6. CURRENT MEASUREMENT SETUP\par
\par
  For completeness, our conversion measurement is already implemented and\par
  verified in production:\par
\par
  - Google tag (AW-18431107276) loaded only after the visitor accepts our\par
    cookie consent banner, blocked entirely otherwise, in compliance with\par
    the Brazilian data protection law (LGPD).\par
  - A "Sign-up" conversion action fires once per created account.\par
  - Our privacy policy declares Google Ads as a data recipient and\par
    describes exactly what is sent.\par
\par
  The API access requested here adds no new data collection from end\par
  users. It only reads back, on our side, the aggregated performance of\par
  the ads we are already paying for.\par
